  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The golden rule: the verb in second place",
     "texto": [
      "In a normal sentence, the conjugated verb always goes in **second position**: **Ich spreche Deutsch** (I speak German).",
      "If you start the sentence with something else, the subject goes after the verb: **Heute spreche ich Deutsch** (today I speak German).",
      "In yes/no questions, the verb goes **first**: **Sprechen Sie Deutsch?**",
      "In questions with a question word, the verb stays in second place: **Wo wohnen Sie?** (where do you live?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs that change their vowel",
     "texto": [
      "Some verbs change their vowel with **du** and with **er/sie**. **Sprechen** (to speak) is one: e → i."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The verb «sprechen» (to speak)",
     "columnas": [
      {
